The fourth inquiry block is installed after `@inquiry-uncertainty-review`. Nine new lessons follow this exact sequence: `inquiry-density-meaning`, `inquiry-cumulative-quantiles`, `inquiry-continuous-moments`, `inquiry-joint-density`, `inquiry-estimation-model`, `inquiry-interval-coverage`, `inquiry-support-and-rivals`, `inquiry-density-study`, `inquiry-density-review`. Earlier finite probability, covariance, mathematical integration and metrology are reused contextually; no shared Record receives a conflicting continuation. Every earlier study/program and all sixteen historical standalone compositions remain intact.

The block develops bounded densities, CDFs, quantiles and affine transformations, positive-probability conditioning, continuous moments and a variance tail bound. It separates density height from probability, probability-zero points from impossible outcomes, and density models from discrete/mixed/singular laws. A product-square construction derives the exact mean distribution of two independent uniform errors: f(z)=(a−|z|)/a² on [−a,a], mean zero and variance a²/6. Geometry, density integration and covariance provide distinct checks. General multivariable integration, unbounded/asymptotic theory and exact-value conditioning retain later preparation.

For Yᵢ=θ+Eᵢ with known half-width a, M=(Y₁+Y₂)/2 is unbiased. The fixed interval M±c has parameter coverage 2c/a−(c/a)² for 0≤c≤a; inverse width is a(1−√(1−p)). The interpretation belongs to repeated data under a fixed parameter and declared model, distinct from posterior probability, prediction or hard bounds. Unknown/fitted a and data-dependent procedures require fresh analysis. A fixed offset gives bias b and mean-square error b²+a²/6; repeated differences cannot separate the offset from θ.

The original synthetic example uses a=2 mm and readings 9 and 23/2 mm. The estimate is 41/4 mm, its 75%-coverage interval is [37/4,45/4] mm, and the support intersection/clipped interval is [19/2,11] mm. Clipping preserves unconditional coverage because the true parameter belongs to the exact-support intersection with probability one under the model; conditional coverage is not asserted. A 95%-coverage width is bracketed by exact rational bisection, with width at most 2/2⁴⁰ mm after forty subdivisions. Identical uniform errors reduce the nominal 75% coverage to 50%; opposite errors give 100%; independent errors with a +1 mm offset give 50%. A pair spanning more than 4 mm contradicts the stipulated exact support. No real measurements or instrument validation are claimed.

